+//
+// ONE LEVEL DEEP, BECAUSE OF DialogButtons. Orca's newer dialogs do not put
+// their buttons in the dialog at all: they build a DialogButtons panel - 38 of
+// them across this GUI - which holds the row and, usefully, gives each button
+// a real wxID_ looked up from its label, so a dialog that used it has better
+// roles than one that did not. The panel is a child of the dialog and the
+// buttons are children of the panel, so a walk that stops at direct children
+// finds nothing whatsoever in the modern half of the application.
